From 9a188ccb8721374231af03655b816de45764298d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:30:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0228 diagnostic: headkey probe logging key/res/doc/doc_b8 at
 the costume-head crash path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two FRAME_STEP cuts in 0x65f520 (the model-definition loader) log the
key-level resource lookup for every head assembly, so the next device run
pins who fills +0xb8 for the per-costume head document (REPORT-LOOKUP-DECODE
§7.3, REPORT-LOG107-CRASH §7.3): at 0x65f8c8 (after bl 0x747300) and at
0x65fb50 (before bl 0x65db60). A shared stub appends a 64-byte record
(res, doc, doc_b8, site, seq, key) to a ring in the frame-step state page
at +0x3300; the host drains it once per present and logs only keys
containing Head. Logging-only: no game state is written, no callee-saved
register or flag is touched, and the replaced instruction runs before the
branch back.

The prescribed runtime guest-code hook is impossible on iOS (hle_cheats.c
alias_setup is compiled out on the iPhone, uw.c's NOP patch is disabled
after it crashed V1.3.5, and the lookup path has no vtable to hook), so
this uses the build-time rewriter cut instead, following the HUD runtime
precedent. nso_asm.py gains the encoders the stub needs (CBZ, MOVZ, LDRB/
STRB post-index, STRB/STRW, LDXR/STXR). Temporary: remove the cuts and the
drain once the log decides pre-register vs route-to-default-head.

Verified: patch_nso.py accepts both cuts (frame_step 5, original bytes
match); the emitted words are byte-identical to the patched image and
disassemble cleanly (0228diag-harness.py); the ring/drain logic passes
against the device-probed Happi/Explorer/Hakama keys (0228diag-harness.c).
No submission, no build triggered.
